  "content": "# codx-junior-ui — interface documentation profile\n\n## Purpose\nThis project is the **codx-junior web UI**. Its wiki documents the product from\nthe screen inward: every section, screen and workflow a user can reach.\n\n## What to document\nFor each UI area:\n- what the screen is for and when a user needs it,\n- the route and entry point (tab, menu, shortcut),\n- the main components and the store/service it talks to,\n- the primary actions and the resulting state changes,\n- permissions, empty states, loading states and error states,\n- links to related screens.\n\nCover at least:\n- application shell, tab bar, desktop/dock and project switcher,\n- chats, agents, profiles and the chat input,\n- Kanban boards, cards, sprints and planning,\n- workspaces, dev containers and previews,\n- teams, company, messenger and meetings,\n- Git view, code review and conflict resolver,\n- browsers, computers and live sessions,\n- knowledge, wiki, settings and account screens.\n\n## Images\nLeave deliberate space for screenshots. Use an HTML placeholder while the image\nfile does not exist (the VitePress build skips it and the page still compiles):\n\n<figure class=\"wiki-image-placeholder\">\n  <div>Image placeholder — Figure 1</div>\n  <figcaption>Figure 1 — Describe the screen, the action and the outcome.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n\nWhen the image file is available, replace the placeholder with:\n\n![Figure 1: Desktop workspace](/images/figure-01-desktop.png)\n\n*Figure 1 — Description of what the screenshot shows and why it matters.*\n\nRules:\n- Number figures per page, use a descriptive filename under `images/`.\n- Always include useful alt text and a caption immediately below.\n- Describe the screen, the action and the outcome.\n- Leave the placeholder/caption pair until the image is supplied.\n- Prefer one focused screenshot per section over galleries.\n\n## Style\n- Write for a user learning the app, not for a frontend compiler.\n- Explain the visible workflow first; mention components and stores after.\n- Use Mermaid for navigation and state flows.\n- Use tables for tabs, shortcuts, settings and permissions.\n- Prefer short pages with links over one giant UI page.\n- Do not include backend implementation details; link to `codx-junior-api`.\n",
